<title>JAPAN: Japan July private machinery orders up 13.6% m/m.</title>
<headline>Japan July private machinery orders up 13.6% m/m.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's private-sector machinery orders, excluding those for machinery at electric power firms and for ships, in July rose a seasonally adjusted 13.6 percent from the previous month to 1.19 trillion yen, the Economic Planning Agency (EPA) said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Month-on-month percentage changes, seasonally adjusted, in different categories of machinery orders were as follows:</p>
<p>			   JULY		 JUNE</p>
<p>   Overall	     +24.4		 -7.6</p>
<p>   Private	     +13.6		 -9.6</p>
<p>(excluding ships, electric utilities)</p>
<p>			   JULY		 JUNE</p>
<p>   Public		+2.0		 -0.6</p>
<p>   External	    +50.9		 -7.1</p>
<p>Year-on-year percentage changes, not adjusted for seasonal factors, in different categories of machinery orders were as follows:</p>
<p>			   JULY		 JUNE</p>
<p>Overall		 +27.2		 -1.6</p>
<p>  Private	     +22.0		 +3.2</p>
<p>   (excluding ships, electric utilities)</p>
<p>			   JULY		 JUNE</p>
<p>  Public		+21.6		 +23.7</p>
<p>  External	    +54.8		 -17.5</p>
</text>
